WEBVTT

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.790
Tempura bowl...

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:16.700
Tempura bowl cravings...

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.120
Tempura... Bowl...

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.370
Um...

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.650
Sir, a-are you all right?

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.430
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:05.430
<b>"Tempura Bowl Survivor"</b>

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:07.160
Hot!

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.080
Are you okay?

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.340
The cheese is so hot.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:15.650
That's all you ever eat these days.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:17.980
I'm hooked on these things.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.120
Want some more coffee?

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.490
Yeah.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.590
Huh, is Toki-kun not here yet?

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:29.280
Oh yeah, he's usually up early.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.510
Maybe it's good to sleep in once in a while.

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.610
<i>Next, we have our Gourmet Guide segment,</i>

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.190
You're right.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.670
<i>where we talk about all the 
restaurants causing a buzz.</i>

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:41.840
<b>Everyone's Favorites! Rice Bowl Special!</b>

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.990
<i>Everyone's Favorites! Rice Bowl Special!</i>

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.640
<i>Satou-san is at the scene. Hello.</i>

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:47.350
<b>Gorgeous Seafood Rice Bowls</b>

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:47.350
<b>Everyone's Favorites!
Rice Bowl Special!</b>

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:47.350
<i>I'm here at the up and coming Shirotake.</i>

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.670
<i>Take a look at this seafood rice bowl.</i>

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:52.100
<b>Gorgeous Seafood Rice Bowls</b>

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:52.100
<b>Everyone's Favorites!
Rice Bowl Special!</b>

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.100
<i>It's filled with all sorts of fresh seafood.</i>

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.470
That looks good.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:55.110
It does.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:03:03.570
<b>Gorgeous Seafood Rice Bowls</b>

00:02:55.110 --> 00:03:03.570
<b>Everyone's Favorites!
Rice Bowl Special!</b>

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:59.530
<i>Shirotake was something of 
a secret until recently,</i>

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.880
<i>but it's exploded since a 
gourmet magazine featured them.</i>

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.940
<i>They're packed every day.</i>

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:09.830
Shirotake...

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.200
You scared me.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:15.960
Shirotake...

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:17.960
Shirotake...

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.110
Shirotake...

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:21.710
T-Tokitaka...

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.330
Shiro... take...

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:22.970
What's wrong?

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:23.720
Shiro...

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:29.600
I went to this shop with the 
pottery class people yesterday.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:31.600
Lucky.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:33.410
But...

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.610
Wh-What a line-up!

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.670
That's for Shirotake?!

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.530
No, I've never seen it this busy before.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.230
Let's just ask them.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:51.140
I'm sorry, it's been like this every day 
since we were featured in a magazine.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:54.780
We'd have to keep you waiting 
for the next three hours.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:56.900
Three hours?

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.940
Three hours?!

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:11.110
So we ended up eating soba 
and going for karaoke

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:13.810
to sing period drama themes.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:19.320
I feel so sorry for you, not being 
able to eat what you wanted.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.870
I get it. I really get it.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:23.830
Was it that disappointing?

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.240
You don't get it?!

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.580
Sui's the type that decides 
what to have on the spot.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.950
But just think about it!

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.550
Wouldn't you be shocked
if you went to a cat café,

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.170
and the cat you wanted
to see was out with a cold?

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.470
<b>Out for the day</b>

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.870
S-Such despair!

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:56.080
See?

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:02.010
Okay, I'll make a ham and cheese
toast for you, then, Tokitaka.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.730
Thank you.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:07.540
I'll make you seafood rice 
bowl latte art, then.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.590
I'll never want to have it again!

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.700
<i>Next, we have tempura bowls.</i>

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.160
<i>Crisp tempura!</i>

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.960
<i>Soaked in sweet sauce, 
topped on steaming rice.</i>

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:24.210
<i>I'm having tempura bowl cravings right now!</i>

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:28.720
<i>My heart was set since I saw it on TV.</i>

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.770
<i>I'm coming for you, tempura bowl!</i>

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.560
Five mitarashi dango.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.950
Three kinako anmitsu.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.530
Eight hana daifuku.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.210
Is something the matter?

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.510
I'm trying to figure out 
how much I have left.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.330
You want to give your customers 
what they want, you know?

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:57.840
So I'm calculating exactly how much 
I need to make not to create any waste.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:58.750
I see.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:05:59.830
That's great.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:03.780
I wouldn't want to leave my 
customers disappointed, either.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:05.960
Absolutely not!

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.610
Hot!

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:12.220
Guys, you need to cool down.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:18.190
<i>It's not entirely a bad thing not 
to get to eat what you want.</i>

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:24.230
<i>But everyone was really looking forward 
to the seafood bowl yesterday.</i>

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.470
I was hoping to get it for them somehow.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.060
Tempura bowl...

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:46.420
Tempura bowl...

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.180
Isn't that...

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:53.050
<i>I only had one sweet bun for lunch.</i>

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.370
<i>I couldn't get off work until 
late because of a meeting.</i>

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:58.180
<i>And the restaurant I was hoping 
to go to was closed for the day.</i>

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:01.190
Tempura bowl...

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.440
Um...

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:03.660
Sir!

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.620
Are you all right?

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.200
I'll call for help right away.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.200
Mini anmitsu set available
Yum!!

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.200
<b>Tempura Bowls!!</b>

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:16.700
Tempura bowl!

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.710
Hey, are you closing already?

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.670
No, you still have some time.

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:23.990
For one, please!

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.420
Right this way, please.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:27.930
Sweet!

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:30.170
<i>I can't believe I'd get to 
have tempura bowl here!</i>

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.350
It's a miracle!

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:34.870
Thank you, God!

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.060
Table for one.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.810
One tempura bowl, please.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:43.490
Tempura bowl?

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:50.860
I'm sorry, sir, we don't 
have tempura bowls here.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:55.200
But it definitely says tempura 
bowl on the sign outside...

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:57.370
<b>Rokuhoudou Recommends

00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.500
<b>Another day of tempura bowl!
Mini anmitsu set available</b>

00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.620
<b>Tempura Bowls!!</b>

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.620
<b>Mini anmitsu set available</b>

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.620
<b>Nice Weather!!</b>

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.290
<i>I misread it...</i>

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.260
<i>Misread it...</i>

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:05.830
<i>Misread it...</i>

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.540
Sir!

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.320
Are you okay?

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.290
Are you sure you aren't ill?

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:14.350
My tempura... bowl...

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:15.360
Huh?

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:18.510
My tempura bowl craving...

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:22.110
The way he's wrought with despair...

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.560
This is us yesterday.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:30.110
<i>He must have lived his entire 
day for a tempura bowl.</i>

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:34.870
Tempura bowl!

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:34.900
<i>Dreaming of the moment he takes a mouthful.</i>

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:40.520
<i>But that dream is about to vanish.</i>

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.710
Sir, one tempura bowl, correct?

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:48.210
But you said you don't have any.

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:50.260
Leave it to me.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:00.970
I want to save...

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:06.640
...your desire.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:30.380
Here you are.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.770
Your tempura bowl.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:35.290
Thank you!

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.050
Time to eat.

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:42.270
It's packed so tightly with tempura 
that you can't even see the rice.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.350
And the shrimp is so huge.

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:48.270
Oh, sorry, that's actually 
chicken tempura, not shrimp.

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:54.100
Ah, I see.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:54.920
Chicken.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:55.750
Right.

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:58.160
<i>He's visibly bummed out.</i>

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.630
Oh, but Tokitaka's chicken tempura...

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:06.630
<i>Oh, whatever, I don't care if it's chicken.</i>

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:09.420
<i>I finally get to have a tempura bowl!</i>

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:36.240
Yum!

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.680
This tempura's so good!

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:40.240
The meat's so soft.

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.240
How did you do this?

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:44.890
Is this really chicken?

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:45.830
Yes.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:50.580
You can make it softer by kneading it 
in yogurt before you put it in the batter.

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.880
It's nice and juicy, isn't it?

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:56.360
Yes. It's not dry at all, 
even though it's breast meat.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:58.220
It's so plump and soft.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:01.800
I've never had chicken tempura like this.

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:09.980
Man, thank you so much.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:12.480
I'm as happy as ever.

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:14.890
I'll never forget what you've done for me.

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:17.230
I'm glad you're happy.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:21.340
Our customers' smiles are 
the source of our strength.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:25.070
Man, Toki-kun's chicken tempura's amazing.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:28.000
I fell in love with that 
chicken tempura, too.

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:32.620
Do you know how Tokitaka-kun discovered it?

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.380
No.

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:38.520
A long time ago, Tokitaka-kun 
went out to buy karaage,

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:40.010
but he couldn't get any.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:44.260
It was that chicken tempura that he 
had when he went to another shop.

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:57.110
He said he was floored 
by how delicious it was.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:11:59.000
I never knew.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.550
To think that tempura would 
save another customer.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:07.060
Maybe it's not always a bad 
thing not to get what you want.

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:13.290
Um... It might really not be a bad thing.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:17.290
<b>Shirotake</b>

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.170
I've been waiting for you.

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:21.840
Thank you for inviting us.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:22.650
Not at all.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:25.560
You've been good to my son. It's nothing.

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:26.990
We just had a cancellation, too.

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:28.430
Don't worry about it.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.770
What did you do, Toki-san?

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.690
Did you save someone? Save a life?

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:36.300
Yeah.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:40.610
No, it's nothing, really.

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.950
Here's your seafood rice bowl.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:47.780
This is it! This is what I've been wanting!

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:50.290
Time to eat.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.290
So good.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.960
Delicious.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:57.790
It is.

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:06.060
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.910
Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori.

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:11.430
<b>"An Incident, Meow"</b>

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:14.340
My, basking in the sunlight, Kinako-chan?

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:16.270
Looks so comfy.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:18.270
We'll be back at the shop soon.

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:27.820
Kinako.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.670
Time for your snack.

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:33.790
It's your favorite, boiled chicken breast.

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:36.350
There you are.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:37.790
Come, Kinako.

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:41.660
What's wrong?

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:43.050
You normally come flying.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:00.730
What was that?

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:03.230
Sui, is something wrong?

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:03.980
That's it.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:04.710
Perfect.

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:05.500
Great.

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:07.740
You're the best. The best.

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.920
Photogenic!

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:14.510
I got the perfect picture.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:21.460
I know, it's a cat party tonight!

00:14:22.430 --> 00:14:23.170
Shoot!

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.170
S-Sui's going to start cooking.

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:28.680
We can't have that, even for 
a cat's welcoming party.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:46.250
Where did he come from?

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:48.570
He's been with Kinako all day, apparently.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:50.560
Do you think he's a stray?

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:51.790
He's not dirty.

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.330
I think he has an owner.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:09.350
Should we ask the public office and 
the customers if they know of an owner?

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:10.340
Yes.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.470
I'll make flyers.

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:15.180
As long as you aren't cooking.

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:17.730
Oh, well.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:21.430
Looks like we're going to have to take 
care of him until we find the owner.

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:23.290
Your face doesn't match your words.

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:40.890
Tenacious, huh?

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:43.290
I never knew that kittens
have so much energy.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.150
Thank you for waiting.

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:51.630
Your matcha pudding and matcha brûlée.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:53.200
Thank you.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:55.590
Okay, two shiratama anmitsu.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:58.770
Sui's jittery today.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:01.000
He must be thinking about the kitten.

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.750
We need to find the owner, quick.

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:08.400
We're all too busy with work 
to take care of him all day.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:11.800
Oh yeah? What's this string for?

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:14.070
I-I just put it in there by accident!

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:16.020
In <i>here</i>?

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.670
It's for playing with the cat, isn't it?

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:19.460
Here's some chicken for you.

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:18.620
No!

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:23.040
<b>Looking for the owner of this cat!
 We discovered him and have taken him in at Rokuhoudou.
 If you have any leads, please contact Rokuhoudou.</b>

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:23.430
Where is the owner?

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.720
We've asked around quite a bit.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:29.110
What shall we do if we don't find the owner?

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:31.490
We could keep him, but...

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:33.020
Are you all right, Kinako?

00:17:34.140 --> 00:17:35.900
He's beat.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:40.400
Huh?

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:41.430
Where's the kitten?

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:44.500
There he is.

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:45.930
Oh, dear.

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:48.040
You were running around 
until just a minute ago.

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:53.010
I wonder what Kinako was like at this age.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:58.010
He was already about his current 
size when he got here.

00:17:58.540 --> 00:17:59.930
That's right.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:04.270
I was shocked when Sui suddenly 
brought him in one day.

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:06.640
Yes.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:12.440
What else do I need to buy?

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:25.120
Come.

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:38.540
Would you like to come to my home?

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:46.290
I hope he wasn't abandoned.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:48.020
Yes.

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:51.580
Well, well.

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:08.310
Excuse me, I heard you've taken in a kitten.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:17.180
I'm sorry for the trouble 
my kitten's caused.

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:18.930
Not at all.

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:20.820
I'm glad we found the owner.

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:24.640
It's thanks to this flyer 
my friend brought me.

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:26.330
The picture is perfect.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:28.730
I knew it was ours the moment I saw it.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:31.540
Wait, this isn't a photo?

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:33.250
Booyah.

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:38.650
With my love and my pixels, 
anything is possible.

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:41.550
<i>Such useless talent.</i>

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:45.550
Sorry my kitten was such 
a nuisance, Kinako-chan.

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:48.220
Thanks for keeping him company.

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:51.570
Come back to hang out.

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:52.310
Of course.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:54.810
Well, let's go home, Denzou.

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:57.820
<b>Denzou</b>

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:55.960
<i>Denzou...</i>

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:57.390
<i>That's a badass name.</i>

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:16.860
For a moment, I thought he might become ours.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:20.590
I was thinking about a name for a bit, too.

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:23.270
Too bad for you.

00:21:23.270 --> 00:21:24.700
You're supposed to be happy.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:26.050
Exactly.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:29.350
Good thing he wasn't abandoned, huh?

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:39.070
I'm glad he had a home to return to.

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:30.380
<b>Next episode</b>

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:30.380
<b>"Love for the Lost Sheep"</b>

00:23:15.920 --> 00:23:20.210
Fancy tempura bowl is nice, but tanuki-don, 
with just the agedama, is nice, too.

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:22.510
Wait, aren't scraps called tenkasu?

00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:23.840
Isn't it agedama?

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:24.880
It's tenkasu.

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:26.540
I'm Team Agekasu.

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:30.380
<b>Come again soon.</b>

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:28.590
What's tanuki-don?

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:29.500
Seriously?!
